{
  "rules": [
    "If sentiment is positive (≥0.2) in the last 3–5 days, model tends to overestimate prices; reduce forecast slope or cap upward momentum.",
    "Model consistently overpredicts early in the 30-day horizon, especially after a recent spike; apply downward bias to first 5–7 days of forecast.",
    "After a sharp price spike (e.g., >85), model often overshoots and fails to correct; cap forecast at +5–10% above peak or use mean-reversion anchor.",
    "When sentiment is low (0.0), model shows weak or flat trend; if true outcome rises sharply, adjust forecast to reflect stronger momentum.",
    "Model underestimates true price volatility in the 15–25 day window; increase forecast variance or add 1–2% upward adjustment for high-sentiment periods."
  ]
}
